= The Impeachment Question

With a Democratic House, serious allegations of abuse of power by the president have reached the point where Congress must decide: investigate, censure, or impeach.

- @impeach_go: Proceed with impeachment
- @impeach_hearings: Hold hearings but not impeach
- @impeach_focus: Focus on the economy

@impeach_go
on-arrival: impeach_done = 1; institutions += 2; subversion_progress -= 0.5; dem_enthusiasm += 0.6; gop_enthusiasm += 1.2; polarization += 3; maga_strength += 1.5; suburban_dem += 1*(1-dissent)

The House impeaches; the Senate acquits along party lines. The country is, if anything, more divided.

@impeach_hearings
on-arrival: impeach_done = 1; institutions += 1; polarization += 1; moderate_strength += 1; progressive_dissent += 5; dem_enthusiasm -= 0.2

Our base feels abandoned; our moderates feel relief.

@impeach_focus
on-arrival: impeach_done = 1; working_dem += 3*(1-dissent); moderate_strength += 2; progressive_dissent += 6; subversion_progress += 0.3

We choose pocketbook politics over process. Critics say we shrank from our duty.
